{"name":"Chalky","hex":"#dfc281","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"chalky","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Consisting of or containing chalk.","Resembling chalk in some way."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chalky"}],"entries":[{"title":"Charles Clinton Fleek","blocks":[{"text":"Charles Clinton \"Chalky\" Fleek was a United States Army soldier and a posthumous recipient of the United States military's highest decoration—the Medal of Honor—for his actions in the Vietnam War."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/ae/Armymoh.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charles_Clinton_Fleek"},{"title":"Chalkdust","blocks":[{"text":"Hollis Urban Lester Liverpool, better known as Chalkdust or Chalkie, is a Trinidad and Tobago calypsonian. He has been singing calypso since 1967 and has recorded more than 300 calypsos."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/93/Dr_Hollis_%22Chalkdust%22_Liverpool_02.jpg/330px-Dr_Hollis_%22Chalkdust%22_Liverpool_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chalkdust"},{"title":"Chalky (comics)","blocks":[{"text":"Chalky was a British comic book character from Cor!!, and from 22 June 1974 when the publications were merged, Buster, both published by IPC. Chalky was created and first drawn by Terry Bave in the 24 July 1971 issue of Cor!!. He was more regularly drawn by Dick Millington and Gordon Hill."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/08/Chalky_comics_book_character.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chalky_(comics)"}],"images":[],"sounds":{"chalky":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/fc/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-chalky.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org